  message: "Rolled up under class item INV-linub-nokij-gibim-rovok-moros-gural-domip-rimof (filed 2026-08-06), which now holds isbefore on this item. NOT a duplicate finding: the class exists because three per-analyzer items share one invariant, and because reading _match_propagation_entry / _lookup_named_entry showed the chain has FOUR links, not one. Emission (L2) is where these items sit; receiver evidence (L3) and the io-boundary F3 gate (L4) are downstream and can refuse an edge that emission successfully adds. So a fix scoped to emission alone can move zero findings while looking like a win at the analyzer. Do not start a fix here until the class measurement fills go/rust/objc and reads the declining branch in each failing analyzer."  # c54b
- op: discuss  # 2364
  at: '2026-08-06T11:31:01Z'  # 2364
  by: agent  # 2364
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2364
  clock: 3  # 2364
  nonce: '2364'  # 2364
  message: "THIS ITEM IS MANUFACTURING INV-busis BLOCKERS - a consequence neither thread recorded, measured 2026-08-06.\n\nINV-busis is held open because the section 3a walk loses track at sites it classifies as GENUINE NON-CALL escapes (field write / container subscript / closure), and that classification is what makes the 7a/7b scope ruling look load-bearing. Measured on hypergumbo self-analysis with the walk reporting its own escape sites (new escape_sites out-param on _ddg_taint_reaches, so nothing re-derives the logic): 24 of 66 resolved escape sites (36.4%) have a CFG node_type of literally `call`, and 99 of 150 escape sites (66.0%) have NO callee recorded at that line. Positive control fires - subprocess.run IS recorded at other sites, so the empties are real absences rather than a dead argument.\n\nThe sites name the mechanism directly: print(, isinstance(stderr, bytes), cmd.append(\"-q\"). Those are calls. This item measured exactly why they carry no edge - python emits ZERO call edges for attribute-chain receivers (cmd.append) and none for a builtin bare Name (print, isinstance). No call edge means no callees_at entry, which means _use_site_terminates cannot decide whether the callee consumes the value, which means escaped=True and the walk returns None.\n\nSO THE IMPACT OF THIS ITEM IS LARGER THAN ITS OWN FILING CLAIMS. The filing sizes it as a FALSE NEGATIVE (a function whose sink calls are all attribute-chain has no sink edge and is never reported) and says the population is unmeasured. That is still true and still the headline. But it ALSO degrades every walk that passes through such a call - the flow is not missed, it is downgraded from a decidable verdict to unknown, which is what holds INV-busis open.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS FOR SEQUENCING: fixing this item is a false-negative fix in the SAFE direction and needs no owner ruling, yet it removes blockers from INV-busis that were being attributed to an ADR-0017 7a/7b scope exclusion. Work it before anything scoped as field-sensitivity.\n\nDIRECTION WARNING for whoever picks it up: emitting these call edges gives callees_at entries, which lets _use_site_terminates start returning True at those sites, which produces MORE False verdicts from the walk. Since PR #214 a False earns sanitized and a sanitized flow is dropped. So this fix can SUPPRESS. Measure on findings, both signs. The WI-joluk coverage gate (merged 2026-08-06) is the guard that makes that safe to attempt.\n\nCAVEATS: python only, self-analysis, not a neutral corpus. The three Go repos available yielded 15 resolved sites between them - too few to share. Instruments: meas/escape_shapes.py, escape_hypergumbo.log."  # 2364
- op: discuss  # 98e3
  at: '2026-08-06T13:05:12Z'  # 98e3
  by: agent  # 98e3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 98e3
  clock: 4  # 98e3
  nonce: '98e3'  # 98e3
  message: "FIX FOR THE ATTRIBUTE-CHAIN HALF, with the direction measured. Premise re-verified on dev 81a62fcf97 with a positive control before any code changed: os.getenv (imported module) 1 edge, helper() in-file 1 edge, obj.bar() attr-on-param 1 edge, print(...) builtin bare Name ZERO, obj.deep.method() attribute chain ZERO. Reproduces this item exactly.\n\nROOT CAUSE NOW LOCALIZED TO A LINE, which this item said it was not. py.py, the catch-all `elif isinstance(func, ast.Attribute)` branch: _unwind_attribute_chain returns a chain for event.organizer.issued_gift_cards.create (root `event` IS an ast.Name), but the emit is gated on `if root_name in module_imports and len(chain_attrs) >= 2`. A chain rooted at a LOCAL fails the first conjunct and falls through with no else, so nothing is emitted. The single-attribute form obj.bar() has emitted an external-module edge since WI-fuvuj for exactly this reason. Depth was the only difference and nothing justified it. FIX: an else that emits python:external:0-0:<method>:unresolved with call_construct=method, placed inside the module-import branch so the class-rooted Django marker (which emits a module-qualified django.db.models edge earlier) keeps winning - pinned by its own test.\n\nI ALSO CORRECTED TWO OF MY OWN CLAIMS BEFORE THEY TRAVELLED.\n(1) I asserted this item suppresses builtins.open sink detection. FALSE. open() DOES emit (python:builtins:0-0:open:unresolved) and matches the catalogued builtins.open host_fs sink - py.py has an EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES whitelist for it. Measured: open YES; print/len/isinstance/eval/exec/input/sorted NO. So the builtin gap is a small whitelist, not builtins in general.\n(2) The two shapes this item names have OPPOSITE directions and must not be fixed as one. ATTRIBUTE CHAIN can miss a catalogued sink (Django obj.related.create) = recall up. BUILTIN BARE NAME mostly turns a call into an escape site; fixing it only helps where a TERMINATING summary exists (print has one, len/isinstance do not), and where it helps it produces MORE False, which since #214 earns sanitized and DROPS a flow = suppressive. Only the attribute-chain half is fixed here. The builtin half is deliberately NOT fixed and should be measured separately.\n\nDIRECTION MEASURED, both signs, on kserve: evidence_rows 22 -> 22, sanitized 0 -> 0, violated verdicts 4 -> 4, methods identical, escape_sites 3 -> 3. ZERO CHANGE. Analyzer level, cache-free: the fix adds 2,155 call edges on kserve/python. So capability moved and adjudication did not - the WI-nonad shape. No suppression introduced, which is the half that mattered.\n\nSTALE-READ CHECK, because byte-identical before/after is the L11 tell: the cache key includes an analyzer-identity hash over every installed .py, and it genuinely differs between the arms (dfb37ba5a9bfc9f9 with the fix, 9fff4c1df3d299e5 without), so both arms analysed fresh. The zero is real.\n\nWHY ZERO HERE AND STILL WORTH LANDING: the 2,155 new edges are logger.info, dict.get, str.replace, argparse.add_argument - none catalogued sinks. The population that WOULD move is Django-shaped (obj.related.create), and pretix, where this item four-adjacent-lines measurement came from, is NOT on this box. So: no measured recall gain on available repos, no suppression, and the false-negative route closed before a repo that exercises it arrives. Same reasoning as WI-joluk.\n\nSTILL UNMEASURED, as the filing says: the size of the population whose sink calls are ALL chain-shaped. This fix makes that population measurable for the first time; it does not size it."  # 98e3
- op: discuss  # 8af2
  at: '2026-08-06T17:21:06Z'  # 8af2
  by: agent  # 8af2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8af2
  clock: 5  # 8af2
  nonce: 8af2  # 8af2
  message: "PR #231 MEASURED, 2026-08-06, AND THE TWO HALVES OF THIS ITEM NOW SEPARATE\nCLEANLY ON TWO REPOS. Instrument: scripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py, which\nruns each call-node escape site of the ADR-0017 section 3a walk through the\nfour stages it can drop out at. Positive control on pretix: 443,296 edges\noffered to _is_taint_call_edge, 191,264 accepted, 69 summary entries, 31,913\ncallees_at entries -- no stage empty, so no cause is reachable by construction.\n\n    cause                                        pretix(17)   hypergumbo(24)\n    1  NO EDGE EMITTED  (this item)                   0         13 (54.2%)\n    3a no receiver type, external placeholder        13 (76.5%)  4 (16.7%)\n    3b resolved first-party, provenance-gated         1          0\n    4a key present, no summary                        2          7 (29.2%)\n    4b summary says propagates (a real escape)        1          0\n\nATTRIBUTE-CHAIN HALF (fixed by #231): WORKS. pretix's call-node escape sites\nare all obj.method() attribute chains -- voucher_list.append(...), p.save(...),\npayment.confirm(), cf.delete(), known_refunds.get(...) -- and ZERO of them lack\nan edge. The emission fix did what it was written to do.\n\nBUILTIN BARE-NAME HALF (deliberately NOT fixed): STILL THE MAJORITY WHERE IT\nAPPLIES. hypergumbo's sites are dominated by print(...), isinstance(...),\nhasattr(...), and 13 of 24 (54.2%) have no edge at all.\n\nSO THE CHANGELOG/thread claim that emission is the blocker is now HALF FALSE\nand should not be carried forward as written: for the fixed shape the wall has\nMOVED DOWNSTREAM to receiver typing (INV-linub). Every pretix stage-3a dst is\npython:external:0-0:NAME:external_symbol -- the literal placeholder --\nand _module_from_symbol_path returns \"\" for it by documented design, so the\nedge can never reach callees_at. #231 emits the edge and the key builder\ndiscards it.\n\nTHE REASON THE BUILTIN HALF WAS HELD BACK IS CORRECT IN PRINCIPLE AND NOT LIVE\nIN PRACTICE. It was deferred as suppressive: builtins.print IS one of the 38\nterminating summaries, so emitting the edge would let _use_site_terminates\nclose the site, produce more False, and since PR #214 a False earns sanitized\nand drops the flow. Measured bound on that fear: there are ZERO barrier-arm\nwalks on any of the four repos that produce walks at all (hypergumbo 36,\npretix 35, prometheus 7, alertmanager 3 -- every invocation on the 3a arm,\nwhere False and None collapse). So fixing the builtin half today would move\nNO finding in either direction. The suppression risk arms when a sanitizer\ncatalogue exists, not before.\n\nRECOMMENDATION, not taken unilaterally: this item's remaining half is now a\nfalse-negative fix with a measured-zero blast radius, which makes it cheap and\nsafe to land NOW rather than after the sanitizer work that would make it\ndangerous. Sequencing that deliberately is the opposite of the usual \"wait\nuntil the risk is understood\" instinct, so it is flagged rather than done."  # 8af2
- op: discuss  # ee1f
  at: '2026-08-06T18:29:52Z'  # ee1f
  by: agent  # ee1f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ee1f
  clock: 6  # ee1f
  nonce: ee1f  # ee1f
  message: "CORRECTION, same day, plus a NEW UNCOVERED SUB-SHAPE this item's\nstatement already covers.\n\nMy note above closed with a recommendation built on a wrong premise: that\nthis item's remaining builtin half is 'cheap and safe NOW, dangerous\nLATER' because a sanitizer catalogue is what arms the suppression hazard.\n\nWHAT I CLAIMED, HOURS EARLIER TODAY: zero barrier-arm walks BECAUSE the\nshipped sanitizer vocabulary is crypto-only -- and therefore \"a sanitizer\ncatalogue ARMS the removal hazard; catalogue growth creates the danger, so\ngates land before catalogue growth.\"\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT ESTABLISHED: I never positive-controlled the zero. A null\nbelieved without demonstrating the instrument can produce a known positive is\nthe exact rule this repo has written down, and I violated it the same day I\nedited it into LIVE.md. It is also the shape of this area's own invalidated\n0.00% confident-negative figure: a tautology of the configuration.\n\nTWO PURPOSE-BUILT FIXTURES, BOTH ZERO WALKS:\n  v1  f = Fernet(key); plain = f.decrypt(tok); cipher = f.encrypt(plain);\n      pathlib.Path(...).write_text(cipher)\n      -> the crypto calls emit python:external:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol.\n         The receiver type is never inferred, so the SOURCE cannot match\n         cryptography.fernet.Fernet.decrypt and the SANITIZER cannot match\n         Fernet.encrypt. No flow exists for a barrier to guard.\n  v2  the same shape written MODULE-QUALIFIED, removing receiver typing as a\n      variable -> source and sanitizer now resolve\n      (python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol), but the\n      SINK emits NO call edge at all: pathlib.Path(...).write_text(x) is an\n      attribute chain rooted at a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT. Still zero walks.\n\nSO THE BARRIER ARM IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE SAME ROOT CAUSE AS THE REST OF THIS\nAREA. Every sanitizer in the shipped catalogue is an INSTANCE METHOD --\nFernet.encrypt, AESGCM.encrypt, AEAD.Seal, Cipher.doFinal -- and\ninstance-method receiver typing is precisely what is broken (INV-linub). That\nis a THIRD symptom family from one root cause, alongside io-boundary catalogue\nreach and the section 4 summary lookup inside the walk.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: the observation (0 barrier walks across 4 repos and 2 fixtures)\nand the practical verdict (an escape reclassification cannot move a finding\ntoday). WHAT DOES NOT: the mechanism, and every sequencing conclusion built on\nit. Catalogue growth CANNOT arm the hazard while receiver typing is broken.\nRECEIVER TYPING IS WHAT ARMS IT.\n\nSTILL OPEN, stated rather than papered over: I could not construct a barrier\nwalk in ANY configuration, so I cannot distinguish \"reachable, and nothing in\nthe corpus hits it\" from \"effectively dead on the DDG path\". There is also NO\nend-to-end test driving the barrier arm through propagate_taint_ddg -- the one\n'sanitized' test uses propagate_taint_structural. A positive control is a\nprerequisite for any future claim about this arm, mine included.\n\nSO THE RECOMMENDATION IS WITHDRAWN AS REASONED. The builtin half's blast\nradius is still measured-zero, but the thing that ends that window is\nRECEIVER TYPING (INV-linub), not catalogue growth -- and INV-linub holds\nisbefore on this item. Landing the builtin half standalone to beat a\ndeadline that does not exist would repeat exactly what PR #231 did.\n\n*** WHAT #231 ACTUALLY BOUGHT, MEASURED. *** On pretix, ZERO of 17\ncall-node escape sites lack an edge -- the attribute-chain half works. On\nhypergumbo, 13 of 24 still have no edge -- the builtin bare-name half is\nuntouched. Findings moved: ZERO. INV-linub predicted precisely this in\nwriting BEFORE #231 landed ('a fix scoped to L2 alone would be measured\nas a win at the analyzer and produce zero new findings'), and held\nisbefore on this item at the time. The prediction was correct and the\nordering was overridden anyway.\n\n*** NEW SUB-SHAPE, IN SCOPE FOR THIS ITEM'S STATEMENT. *** A chain rooted\nat a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT emits no call edge at all:\n  pathlib.Path('/tmp/out.bin').write_text(cipher)   -> NO calls edge\nOnly 'instantiates -> python:pathlib:0-0:Path' is emitted; the\n.write_text(...) on the result is invisible. #231 fixed chains rooted at\na LOCAL; a chain rooted at a call result is a distinct sub-shape and is\nstill open. This is what killed barrier fixture v2 -- the sink vanished.\nIt matters beyond taint: Path(...).write_text is an ordinary Python idiom\nand every catalogued sink reached that way is currently unreachable."  # ee1f
- op: discuss  # 418f
  at: '2026-08-06T22:05:03Z'  # 418f
  by: agent  # 418f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 418f
  clock: 7  # 418f
  nonce: 418f  # 418f
  message: "BARRIER-ARM MECHANISM CORRECTED A SECOND TIME, 2026-08-06 (dev 8b1a20cc1b,\nfiled as INV-funit). This thread carries a correction from earlier the same\nday saying \"receiver typing arms the suppression hazard, not catalogue\ngrowth\". THAT IS ALSO WRONG and is retracted; it was the second uncontrolled\naccount of the same zero.\n\nESTABLISHED WITH A POSITIVE CONTROL, which neither prior account had: the\nbarrier arm was blocked by _register_sanitizer_callers reading the NAME slot\nof the dst for receiver evidence that production analyzers put in the MODULE\nslot. The comparison was \"cryptography.fernet.Fernet.encrypt\" == \"encrypt\" --\nfalse by construction for every method-shaped sanitizer, i.e. the entire\nshipped catalogue -- so the INV-finoh call_construct==\"method\" refusal was\nunconditional in production.\n\nTwo probes differing ONLY in receiver form emit a BYTE-IDENTICAL dst\n(python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:encrypt:external_symbol) and differ\nonly in meta.call_construct; that alone flipped sanitizer_lines from\n{(handler,'plaintext'): [7,7,7,7]} to {}. The idiomatic form reported\n\"violated\" at \"precise\" confidence about code that visibly encrypts, and now\nreports \"confirmed\" with the arm firing.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES FROM BOTH RETRACTED ACCOUNTS: WI-joluk's coverage gate landing\nbefore removal authority is still right. The section 3a arm still tests\n`is True`, so escape-reclassification and section 7a field sensitivity are\nstill structurally INERT for finding counts. INV-karud clause (b)'s zero is\nstill not independent corroboration.\n\nWHAT IS NEW AND DECISION-RELEVANT: the corpus holds ZERO plaintext sanitizer\ncall sites (pretix's single gate-reaching edge is a bare `encrypt`, correctly\nrefused; everywhere else is absence), and the module slot reaches taint only\nfor python and java. The sanitizer/barrier machinery has no live surface on\ntoday's corpus -- everything here is prevention whose value scales with a\ncatalogue that is not growing. That belongs in the exit-condition package."  # 418f
- op: discuss  # 8e68
  at: '2026-08-08T21:03:19Z'  # 8e68
  by: agent  # 8e68
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8e68
  clock: 8  # 8e68
  nonce: '8e68'  # 8e68
  message: "TWO STATEMENT CLAIMS ARE FALSE. Refile before working this item.\n\n(1) \"self.<field>.<method>() emits NO CALL EDGE AT ALL\" -- FALSE at population\n    scale. 2,774 of 3,418 sites (81.2%; independently replicated at 83.1%) DO\n    emit, via the WI-hiziz Site-3 inherited-field branch, carrying the `external`\n    placeholder. Only 578-581 (~17%) emit nothing -- OWN fields failing the\n    guard (e.g. pretix pdf.py:797 self.background_file.read()). The correct claim\n    is \"emits an edge with NO RECEIVER EVIDENCE\", which is INV-linub's clause,\n    not an emission gap. NOTE: a single hand fixture using an own field\n    reproduces the 17% case and looks like the general case -- that is how this\n    claim survived.\n\n(2) The DOMINANT no-edge shape is the CONSTRUCTOR / CALL-RESULT ROOT\n    (`Path(...).rglob(p)`), 8,767 sites = 80.0% of the no-edge population and\n    100% of that shape. It appears nowhere in the statement or root_cause --\n    only in a late discussion note.\n\nPOPULATION (7 Py repos, unique (file,line,name) catalogue-name call sites):\n  no edge at all = 10,957 / 49,811 = 22.0% (replicated 22.1% and 22.4%)\n  EXCLUDING sqlalchemy = 15.2%. sqlalchemy contributes 16,725 sites (32.9%) with\n  ZERO catalogue entries -- an L1 catalogue gap, not an emission gap. Both this\n  item's and INV-linub's blocker sizings are ~2.9x inflated by it.\n\nPR #231's shape (chain rooted at a local) is CONFIRMED FIXED: 11,268/11,404 =\n98.8% emit.\n\nORDERING CONSTRAINT: do NOT emit for ctor-roots before the constructor's type is\ncarried. Alone it converts 8,767 silences into 8,767 evidence-free `external`\nedges reaching 0 catalogue entries -- the measured #231 / WI-nonad outcome\n(emission improved, findings moved zero)."  # 8e68
- op: discuss  # e8e2
  at: '2026-08-09T01:53:25Z'  # e8e2
  by: agent  # e8e2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e8e2
  clock: 9  # e8e2
  nonce: e8e2  # e8e2
  message: "CORRECTION to the 2026-08-08 note on this thread, which is replicated verbatim on\nINV-linub, INV-mumov and WI-zilag. Adjudicated by four independent measurement lenses\nplus three adversarial refuters each; the numbers below are only those that survived\nrefutation, and the refuted ones are named at the bottom so they are not re-cited.\n\n1. \"32.9% of the measured population (sqlalchemy, 16,725 sites)\" IS A COHORT ARTIFACT,\n   NOT A CATALOGUE GAP. The sqlalchemy REPO was one of the 7 repos measured (pretix,\n   sqlalchemy, mitmproxy, poetry, pyright, meson, kserve). All 16,994 rows in the\n   sqlalchemy artifact carry file paths under ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/sqlalchemy/,\n   and the instrument's own REPOS constant names it. It was never call sites INTO\n   sqlalchemy-as-a-dependency. Confirmed independently by three lenses; that 7-repo\n   cohort contains ZERO sqlalchemy consumers, so it could not have tested the other\n   reading even in principle.\n\n2. \"it inflates the blocker ~2.9x\" IS WRONG FOR REACH. The true factor is 1.47x\n   (50,772 population) / 1.48x (49,811). The genuine 2.9x belongs to a DIFFERENT\n   family -- CALL_RESULT_ROOT no-edge, 8,962 total of which sqlalchemy is 5,826 =\n   2.86x, which is INV-mumov's territory. The factor was computed on one family and\n   applied to another.\n\n3. \"ZERO catalogue entries -- unreachable at L1\" IS DIAGNOSTICALLY WRONG. sqlalchemy\n   has 88-93 REACHING sites (builtins.open 20, os.path.exists 11, os.remove 11). Its\n   denominator is dominated by short-name COLLISIONS with catalogue entries -- execute\n   3,228, all 1,721, order_by 1,362, filter, get, commit -- whose only catalogue homes\n   are django.db.models / sqlite3. Those sites MUST NOT reach. 52.7% of them are in\n   ambiguous_names. The remedy for a collision is not a catalogue entry.\n\n4. TWO POPULATIONS, ONE PROBE -- name one and stay in it. 50,772 (plain\n   (file,line,name) dedup) and 49,811 (agg2.py's uniq()) come from the same row set\n   under two aggregation rules, reproduced 7/7 per repo in both directions. PREFER\n   50,772 AND SAY SO: uniq() DELETES BOTH MEMBERS of a colliding site, dropping 961\n   distinct sites that are reach-depleted (8.1% vs 16.06%), so 49,811 is the truncated\n   population and mildly INFLATES every reach rate.\n\n5. NEW, AND IT UNDERCUTS THE L4 FIGURES ON THIS THREAD: django.db.models-stamped sites\n   reach at 4,623/4,623 = 100.00% BY CONSTRUCTION -- py.py:527 hard-codes the module\n   string, python.yaml holds the same 29 names, and _module_matches on identical\n   strings is unconditionally True. That family is 57.3% of the reach numerator. Strip\n   it and L4-admit-given-evidence falls 78.69% -> 61.22%. The 87.0% D3 figure is\n   pretix at 99.34% against 54.84% for the other six repos. Do not quote 78.6%/87.0%\n   as a general result.\n\n6. INV-mumov's \"15.2%\" reproduces from NO candidate denominator any lens tried. Treat\n   it as unsourced.\n\nREFUTED 3/3, DO NOT RE-CITE: a \"cross-instrument splice\" between two different probes\n(there is one probe, two aggregation rules); and the whole \"no long tail / 2.53%\nthird-party / bounded curation\" family -- its census admits a site only if the method\nname is ALREADY in python.yaml, which excludes by construction every name curation\nwould add, and adding two out-of-cohort repos moved distinct third-party packages\n52 -> 88 with no saturation.\n\nARTIFACT INTEGRITY: the run that produced the 32.9%/23.0% anchor (inv8/denom-inference)\ncarries an ENOSPC traceback in its own log. The per-repo rows are self-consistent and\nreproduce, but that artifact was written under the WI-kovoj disk trap.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE WORK: there is no L1 catalogue fix to make here. The real\nuser-facing defect found while adjudicating this paragraph is filed separately as\nINV-fibis (verify-claims returns `confirmed` for a boundary reachable through modules\nthe catalogue cannot adjudicate -- reproduced on poetry and full-stack-fastapi-template\nwith a positive control firing in the same run)."  # e8e2
- op: discuss  # e3d5
  at: '2026-08-09T23:07:47Z'  # e3d5
  by: agent  # e3d5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e3d5
  clock: 10  # e3d5
  nonce: e3d5  # e3d5
  message: "CONSTRUCTOR-RESULT ROOT SUB-SHAPE CLOSED FOR PYTHON, PR #254. Item stays violated;\nthis closes one shape, not the invariant.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG. PR #253 taught the receiver resolver that a constructor call carries a\ntype, but wired it into the two ASSIGNMENT call sites only. So the type existed and the\nEMISSION site never asked for it: Path(raw).write_text(x) emitted no call edge in any\nbranch and tagged ZERO io-boundaries, while the identical p = Path(raw);\np.write_text(data) tagged one. Verified on the shipping tree with a positive control\nfiring in the same run, so the zero was real and not an instrument fault.\n\nTWO GAPS, WHICH IS WHY A ONE-LINE CHANGE COULD NOT CLOSE IT. (1) the emission site\ncalled _derived_receiver_module without the constructor resolver, so\n(Path(raw) / \"o\").write_text(x) could not type its root; (2) _derived_receiver_module\nanswers \"what does this DERIVATION preserve\", and a bare Path(raw) is the ROOT, not a\nderivation -- no branch matched it. Fixing only (1) leaves the commonest shape broken.\n\nFIX SHAPE, recorded because this item's own root_cause field asks whether the declining\nbranches share one shape. They did: the answer to \"what type does this receiver\nexpression have\" was being given privately inside _preserved_receiver_type, so the\nemission site could only ask a narrower question. It is now ONE predicate\n(_receiver_type) with both callers routed through it, and _external_constructor_type\nmoved to module level so the emission site inherits the INV-kipor binding check instead\nof growing a second copy. TYPE_PRESERVING_MEMBERS still gates propagation separately, so\nwidening which receivers carry a type did not widen which members preserve it.\n\nMEASURED THROUGH PRODUCTION, instrument in-repo at\nscripts/measure-ctor-root-typing-ab.py, positive control printed first (0 -> 1 boundary\non a known-positive fixture, so the corpus numbers are not uncontrolled nulls):\n\n  +125 boundary chains, +260 typed call edges, +260 total edges -- every new edge\n  NET-NEW, zero re-keyed.\n  meson +89, mitmproxy +14, poetry +7, kserve +6, sqlalchemy +5, pretix +4, pyright +0.\n\nTWO POPULATIONS, NAMED because they are not the same number. The static census counts\n128 reaching SITES; the A/B counts 125 boundary CHAINS. tag_io_boundaries collapses\nsame-caller-same-primitive sites -- mitmproxy's test_init_dir calls Path(mydir).exists()\ntwice in one function and that file is duplicated under examples/ and\ndocs/src/examples/, which is the ENTIRE 3-count difference. Chased down rather than\nreported as a 2.3% discrepancy.\n\nSCOPE, so this is not read as more than it is. 269 of 27,354 call-result-root sites\nacross the 7-repo cohort are typeable (~1%), and 128 reach the catalogue. meson alone\nsupplies 89 of the 125 chains (71.2%) -- NOT an evenly distributed win, and it does not\nsupport a general \"Python gains ~125 boundaries\" claim.\n\nDIRECTION. The suppression direction measured ZERO on hypergumbo's own claims:\ncheck-self-claims byte-identical across the change (18 claims / 16 inconclusive /\n2 violated) against a snapshot recorded pre-fix, so a real A/B and not a re-run. THAT\nZERO IS WEAK AND IS NOT EVIDENCE OF SAFETY -- one repo, and the barrier arm (the only\nconsumer of a False) measures zero walks on every repo tried, so this change has not\nbeen observed under the conditions where it could suppress a finding.\n\nWHAT REMAINS OPEN IN THIS FAMILY, measured rather than asserted. ~27,085 of the 27,354\ncall-result-root sites have receivers of genuinely UNKNOWN type and still emit no edge.\nThat is deliberate, not an oversight: PR #231 measured that emitting an untyped edge\nmoves ZERO findings, so minting them would be capability without recall. A related\nasymmetry ships disclosed and pinned as a passing test -- an unknown receiver emits an\nuntyped `external` placeholder when ASSIGNED and nothing when INLINE. Both tag zero\nboundaries (verified, not assumed). Re-evaluation trigger recorded in\ntest_py_ctor_root_receiver_typing.py: revisit if a consumer is ever added that\ndistinguishes \"no edge\" from \"an edge to an untyped receiver\".\n\nNOT CITED HERE, DELIBERATELY: this thread's neighbours carry two conflicting accounts of\nwhether self.<own field>.<method>() emits edges (a plan note says zero; the 2026-08-08\nunconfounded re-measurement on this item says self.field DOES emit at 81-83%). I did not\nmeasure that shape in this work and take no position on it. Whoever picks it up should\nre-measure rather than inherit either number.\n\nTagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: the +125 chain figure is a quantitative improvement\nclaim and belongs in the validation queue."  # e3d5
