- op: discuss  # 4085
  at: '2026-08-10T07:44:05Z'  # 4085
  by: agent  # 4085
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4085
  clock: 12  # 4085
  nonce: '4085'  # 4085
  message: "S8 RE-MEASUREMENT, 2026-08-10: this item is now the LARGEST single cause of section 3a\nescape, measured rather than argued.\n\nscripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py on hypergumbo's own tree (dev ecb954eb05), positive\ncontrol passing (595,736 edges offered / 317,528 accepted / 29,301 callees_at entries):\nof the 26 CALL-node escape sites, **13 (50.0%) are \"NO EDGE EMITTED\"** -- this item's\nterritory. The next cause is a section 4 summary-catalogue gap at 30.8%, and receiver\ntyping (INV-linub) is down to 15.4% after seven python PRs plus the go composite-literal\nfix.\n\nWHY THAT ORDERING MATTERS FOR WHOEVER PICKS THIS UP. This item's own filing, and\nINV-linub's, both record that an L2-only emission fix measures as a win at the analyzer\nand moves ZERO findings, because an edge arriving with no receiver type is refused at\nthe F3 gate. PR #231 demonstrated exactly that. So \"50% of call escapes are missing\nedges\" is NOT a licence to emit them: it is a statement that emission and typing have to\nland together for these 13 sites, and the direction must be measured on findings.\n\nDIRECTION WARNING, unchanged and still live: emitting these edges populates callees_at,\nwhich lets _use_site_terminates decide sites it currently has to treat as escapes, which\nproduces MORE False verdicts -- and since PR #214 a False earns `sanitized` and DROPS the\nflow. WI-joluk's coverage gate exists for this and is wired to the BARRIER arm only.\n\nSAMPLE CAVEAT: one repo, python only, 26 call-node sites. Not a cohort."  # 4085
- op: discuss  # b032
  at: '2026-08-17T02:07:13Z'  # b032
  by: agent  # b032
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b032
  clock: 13  # b032
  nonce: b032  # b032
  message: "HEADLINE REFUTED, STATEMENT NOW HOLDS ON THE FILED SHAPE, ITEM STAYS OPEN FOR A\nDIFFERENT REASON. Measured 2026-08-16, dev 0d305fe0e4, production analyze_python\non a purpose-built fixture isolating four receiver shapes.\n\nTHE TITLE SAYS \"Python analyzer emits ZERO call edges for attribute-chain\nreceivers (obj.related.create())\". It emits.\n\n    shape                             module slot     construct  edge?\n    p = Path(raw); p.write_text(x)    pathlib.Path    method     yes\n    Path(raw).write_text(x)           pathlib.Path    method     yes\n    obj.related.create()              external        method     YES   <- filed shape\n    obj.store.path.write_text(raw)    external        method     yes\n\nThis item's STATEMENT -- \"Every call site of a catalogued taint source or sink in\nPython produces a calls edge, regardless of the receiver syntax used to reach the\ncallee\" -- is satisfied on all four shapes I tested. I did NOT enumerate every\nreceiver syntax, so this is evidence on the filed shape plus three neighbours,\nnot a proof over the syntax space.\n\nWHY THE ITEM IS STILL LIVE, AND WHY IT SHOULD NOT BE CLOSED ON THE ABOVE. The\nuser-visible consequence the item was filed for -- \"an all-attr-chain function\nhas NO sink edge and its flow is never reported\" -- still holds, by a DIFFERENT\nmechanism. The attribute-chain edges carry module slot 'external': no receiver\nevidence. io_boundary.gate_named_entry then correctly drops method-kind entries\nfor want of a module hint, so the sink is still unreachable. The failure moved\nfrom L2 (emission) to L3 (evidence) in INV-linub's chain vocabulary.\n\nThat distinction is the whole point of INV-linub and it decides the fix: nothing\nfurther is owed by the emission path, and an emission-shaped fix would now be a\nno-op. What is owed is receiver typing for ATTRIBUTE chains -- the constructor\nchain already has it (Path(raw).write_text(x) carries pathlib.Path and MATCHES,\nwhich is new since this item was filed and is why python is now the only\nlanguage clean on all three chain_probe sites).\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE awaits_bakeoff_validation TAG: the quantitative claim this\nitem carries should be re-read before the queue is drained against it. A bakeoff\nlooking for \"attribute-chain call edges appear\" will find them and may read that\nas the item moving, when the finding-level metric will not have moved at all.\n\nSUGGESTED RESHAPE, not applied: retitle to name the L3 gap (attribute-chain\nreceivers carry no module hint, so catalogued method-kind sinks stay unreachable)\nand let the emission clause close. Left for whoever next works it, since the\nretitle changes what the awaits_bakeoff_validation queue is measuring."  # b032
