  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nTHE SUGGESTED RESHAPE IS APPLIED, and the refutation is independently reproduced rather than inherited from this thread. Production analyze_python on a fixture at dev 11a240f83d:\n\n    obj.related.create(x)   EDGE EMITTED, call_construct=method, module slot 'external'\n    obj.decode()            EDGE EMITTED, call_construct=method\n    os.remove(x)            EDGE EMITTED, module slot 'os'\n    print(x) / len(x) / undefined_fn(x)   NO EDGE  (that is INV-foluz, a different item)\n\nSo the title's 'emits ZERO call edges for attribute-chain receivers' is false at tip. Retitled to name the L3 gap that IS live: the edge arrives with no receiver evidence, io_boundary.gate_named_entry correctly refuses a method-kind entry for want of a module hint, and the sink stays unreachable. Same user-visible consequence, different mechanism, different fix.\n\nWHY THE RETITLE IS NOT COSMETIC -- IT CHANGES WHAT A QUEUE MEASURES. This item carries awaits_bakeoff_validation. A bakeoff draining that queue against the OLD title would look for 'attribute-chain call edges appear', find them, and read the item as moved -- while the finding-level metric has not moved at all. The item's own 08-17 entry flagged exactly this and left the retitle to whoever next worked it."  # ebb4
