  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GOVERNING MEASUREMENT. docs/measurements/0001-taint-flow-precision.md puts taint-flow precision at ~41% population-weighted across six real repositories. Per WI-sivuz's PRE-REGISTERED decision bands -- named before any interval was computed, so the interval cannot be used to move them -- that is the <50% band: \"precision is the headline problem and recall work should stop until it is understood.\"\n\nP1 -> P2. Same family: this is now (after today's retitle) an L3 recall gap -- attribute-chain receivers carry no module hint, so catalogued method-kind sinks stay unmatchable. Making them matchable adds flows at ~41% precision.\n\nNOTE FOR THE awaits_bakeoff_validation QUEUE: this item still carries that tag, and the re-rank does not strip it. What changed today is what the tag is measuring (see the retitle entry)."  # 7c70
