  nonce: '0e11'  # 0e11
  message: "PARTIAL, PR #752 (dev d0080868c6): the CONSTRUCTOR-typed slice of this item's\nL3 gap. An imported PascalCase name that is called now types its instance\n`<module>.<Class>` in both the assigned and inline forms\n(`_imported_class_instance`, consulted after the I/O constructor table), so\n`f = Fernet(key); f.decrypt(t)` carries `cryptography.fernet.Fernet` where it\ncarried `external`. What stays open under this item: ATTRIBUTE chains rooted\nat a typed object (`obj.related.create()`), which need the attribute's type\nfrom the class field maps -- filed as the next slice, not folded here.\nMEASURED: mitmproxy 22,320 -> 23,429 sites (315 typed, 0 lost); poetry 15,345 -> 16,263 (186 typed, 0 lost, 3 re-keys); pretix 69,755 -> 78,852 sites (748 typed, 0 lost, 0 re-keys); io-boundaries byte-identical on mitmproxy / poetry / meson (534 / 190 / 2,873); crypto reach on real code: mlflow utils/crypto.py:350 and litellm app_crypto.py:32 go python:external:0-0:decrypt -> ...aead.AESGCM.decrypt, accepted by the production source matcher."  # 0e11
- op: discuss  # 063f
  at: '2026-09-04T04:49:05Z'  # 063f
  by: agent  # 063f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 063f
  clock: 24  # 063f
  nonce: 063f  # 063f
  message: "Attribute-chain slice shipped in PR #756 (dev a21ef3223f). `obj.field.method()` where `obj` is a project class whose `__init__` typed `field` with a catalogued constructor now carries that module in the slot, from any file: `_receiver_type` answers a dotted field path from `external_var_types`, the walker binds `<local>.<field>` keys at the binding site (purged on rebind, pruned with a shadowed root, one hop through a project-class field, `self.<field>.<field>` too). Structural finding from the red tests: the per-class field maps were built INSIDE `_extract_edges` per file, so a class imported from another file had no map at all; they are now built once per repo before any file's edges (`_collect_class_field_maps`, keyed by class-symbol id) with the per-file param-type resolvers factored into `_make_param_type_helpers`. Side effect: a DERIVATION rooted at `self.<field>` (`self.out_dir / name`) is typed for the first time — the key existed but only the self-branch emitter read it. Measured (lab: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mumov_attrchain_09032026/): io-boundaries A→B python io chains poetry 190→191, mitmproxy 534→535, meson 2873→2880, pretix 1093→1093 (9 new `pathlib.Path` rows, 0 lost, every one read back at source); per-site churn poetry 4 gains / meson 11 / mitmproxy 7 / pretix 0, 0 losses, 0 re-keys, every moved row read back at source. NOT closed by this slice: a factory FUNCTION returning a catalogued type (`sqlite3.connect(p)` — the derived constructor table holds `sqlite3.Connection`, the class) is the return-type-registry consumer's job (INV-dihos python phase). Status stays violated until the bakeoff validates (awaits_bakeoff_validation kept)."  # 063f
