  message: "TAG STRIPPED, ITEM STAYS VIOLATED — and now with a measured population instead of an\nestimated one (2026-09-04 bakeoff-queue drain).\n\nTHE EMISSION CLAUSE IS CLOSED, verified by re-running THIS ITEM'S OWN persisted instrument\n(`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/py_zero_edge_check.py`, whose positive\ncontrol -- `os.getenv` -- passed in the same run, so a harness fault is distinguishable from\nan analyzer fault). Against the table this item filed:\n\n    shape                      filed   today\n    print(...)      builtin      0       2 sites -> 2 edges   (python:builtins:...:print)\n    obj.deep.method()  chain      0       2 sites -> 2 edges\n    obj.bar()       attr param    3       3\n    helper()        in-file       2       2\n\nThe title already records the emission clause as REFUTED; this is the confirmation on the\nfiled fixture rather than on an adjacent one.\n\nTHE L3 HALF IS OPEN AND NOW SIZED. Python method-call edges carrying a REAL module rather\nthan the `external` sentinel, six cold repos:\n\n    pretix      6,409 / 31,669   (20%)   25,260 on the sentinel\n    beads         370 /    894   (41%)      524\n    hypergumbo 16,472 / 37,081   (44%)   20,609\n\nSo on the Django repository this item was filed from, four in five python method-call edges\nstill cannot reach a catalogued row. That is the item's real remaining population, and it is\na number now instead of \"plausibly large, but I did NOT size it and will not guess\".\n\nWHY THE TAG COMES OFF ANYWAY: the tag tracks whether a shipped quantitative claim moved.\nPR #756's did -- on the filed fixture, measured above. The residual is the item's own open\nhalf, tracked by its status (violated), not by a validation tag.\n\nA CAUTION FOR WHOEVER TAKES THE L3 HALF, earned this session: four consecutive\nreceiver-typing changes (#765, #768, #769, #772) moved io-boundaries by ZERO on every\nrepository measured, because the io classifier already matches by SHORT NAME when the module\nslot is empty. Filling the slot buys PRECISION, not recall. Do not size this item's payoff\nin io findings without first finding a repository where the short-name gate refuses.\n\nArtifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_queue_09042026/PHASE4_RESULTS.md"  # e1e3
- op: update  # 1c89
  at: '2026-09-04T17:54:58Z'  # 1c89
  by: agent  # 1c89
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1c89
  clock: 27  # 1c89
  nonce: 1c89  # 1c89
  set:  # 1c89
    fields:  # 1c89
      statement: "A call site of a catalogued method-kind I/O primitive in Python carries, in its edge's module slot, the STATIC OWNER PATH of the receiver -- the type of the object the method is called on (ADR-0051) -- so that the shared F3 gate can reach the catalogue row. A receiver whose type is not derivable leaves the 'external' sentinel in the slot and the row stays unreachable. (SUPERSEDED CLAUSE, kept for the record: this field previously read \"Every call site of a catalogued taint source or sink in Python produces a calls edge, regardless of the receiver syntax used to reach the callee.\" That EMISSION claim is satisfied at tip and was refuted in the title on 2026-08-17; the item never rewrote the field to match.)"  # 1c89
      root_cause: "LOCALIZED, and no longer an emission defect. py.py emits a calls edge for every receiver syntax measured (attribute chain, attr-on-param, imported module, builtin bare Name). The live gap is the module slot: it is filled by the receiver-typing path (_receiver_type / _imported_class_instance / external_var_types); where the receiver's type is not derivable from an import-and-construct (PR #752), a project-class field map (PR #756) or an annotation, the slot degrades to the 'external' sentinel, and io_boundary.gate_named_entry (io-boundary:F3, the decision SHARED by lookup_with_module and taint's _lookup_named_entry) correctly refuses a method-kind row for want of an owner path. Uncovered producers, each owned elsewhere: a factory FUNCTION returning a catalogued type (INV-dihos, python phase) and any chain whose root is not an ast.Name (INV-luhug). STALE CLAUSES REMOVED: the field previously asserted \"analyze_python emits no calls edge when the callee is an attribute chain whose root is not an imported module\" and \"none for a builtin bare Name (print())\" -- the first was refuted 2026-08-17, the second by PR #711 (INV-foluz), and the 2026-09-02 entry on this item flagged the residue without editing the field."  # 1c89
- op: discuss  # a18a
  at: '2026-09-04T17:54:58Z'  # a18a
  by: agent  # a18a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a18a
  clock: 28  # a18a
  nonce: a18a  # a18a
  message: "FIELDS BROUGHT INTO LINE WITH THE ITEM, 2026-09-04, dev ef9c55f8bf. No status change, no re-prioritisation, no new work: this is the rewrite that three earlier entries on this thread asked for and none performed.\n\nWHY IT WAS OWED. The title has recorded the emission clause as REFUTED since 2026-08-17, but the statement and root_cause fields still described emission. The 2026-08-23 entry said in terms: \"This item's own STATEMENT is about whether a calls edge is EMITTED at all ... Re-read and if necessary rewrite the statement BEFORE closing; closing on the title would be closing on the wrong claim.\" The 2026-09-02 entry then noted the root_cause's bare-Name sentence had gone stale too, and left it. An item whose statement names a satisfied clause is one closure-evidence check away from being closed on the wrong claim, which is the failure mode INV-nufob already supplied.\n\nRE-VERIFIED AT TIP BEFORE REWRITING -- production analyze_python, one fixture, control in the same run:\n\n    obj.write(p)              line 6  -> python:external:0-0:write:unresolved     cc=method\n    obj.deep.chain.write(p)   line 7  -> python:external:0-0:write:unresolved     cc=method\n    os.remove(p)              line 8  -> python:os:0-0:remove:unresolved          cc=method   <- CONTROL\n    print(p)                  line 9  -> python:builtins:0-0:print:unresolved\n\nL2 holds on all four shapes. L3 is live on both chain shapes, and the control shows the slot is filled when the owner path is derivable, so the empties are real absences rather than a dead harness.\n\nWHAT THE FIELDS NOW SAY: statement names the owner-path (L3) clause; root_cause names the receiver-typing path, the two shipped slices that narrowed it (#752, #756), the shared F3 gate that refuses without a hint, and the two uncovered producers that are owned elsewhere (INV-dihos python phase, INV-luhug). The superseded text is quoted in the statement rather than deleted, so a reader who arrives from an old citation can see what moved.\n\nUNCHANGED: status violated, P2 (the WI-sivuz band re-rank of 2026-08-17, which the 2026-09-03 band reading did not reverse on this item), and the 2026-09-04 sizing -- pretix 6,409/31,669 (20%), beads 370/894 (41%), hypergumbo 16,472/37,081 (44%) python method-call edges carrying a real module rather than the sentinel."  # a18a
- op: discuss  # 5d2a
  at: '2026-09-06T15:50:16Z'  # 5d2a
  by: agent  # 5d2a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5d2a
  clock: 29  # 5d2a
  nonce: 5d2a  # 5d2a
  message: "PHASE 6 SCOPING CENSUS 2026-09-06 (dev 278d1c5fed), reporting only -- no status change, no slice chosen yet. The arc's Phase 6 opened today (gate lifted on 0012); before choosing an L3 slice, the RECEIVER SHAPES behind this item's population were counted, because the class entry of 2026-09-04 says an L3 fix is measured through the taint path and pays in precision, so the slice must be the shape that is both large and TYPEABLE.\n\nPOPULATION: every python taint call edge (production _is_taint_call_edge) whose dst is `python:external:0-0:<name>:external_symbol` with call_construct=method, on the two python repos of the 9-repo cohort surveyed at tip: pretix 25,260 + kserve 2,427 = 27,687; 27,599 joined to the source AST by (file, line, method name). Instrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/linub_pyshapes_09062026/census.py (tree-sitter via the language pack, the analyzer's own grammar).\n\n    receiver shape                                    edges   of which the NAME is a catalogued method-kind primitive\n    self.<attr> chain  (self.client.get, self.event.save)   5,675   3,755\n    attr chain rooted at a local name (a.b.m())        4,533   2,573\n    call result, function  (f().m(), a.f().m())        4,025   1,926\n    bare name = parameter                              3,358   1,948\n    self / cls                                         1,922      25\n    name bound by `x = a.f()`                          1,868     679\n    literal receiver (\"...\".format etc.)               1,554      14\n    bare name, unbound in the function (global/import) 1,358     305\n    name bound by other rhs                              786     184\n    name bound by `x = f()`                              489      89\n    subscript                                            444      98\n    loop variable                                        375     158\n    name bound by `x = Constructor()`                    248      67   <- the #752 shape's residue (non-imported / non-PascalCase constructors)\n    attr chain rooted at subscript / call / other        390     247\n    with-as, parenthesized, comprehension                141      24\n\nTOP CATALOGUED NAMES ON THESE EDGES: get 2,665, save 1,819, post 1,309, create 1,254, filter 655 -- Django ORM and HTTP-client spellings. So \"names a catalogued method\" here is overwhelmingly a NAME COLLISION that the ambiguous gate already refuses (the row is requests/httpx `get`/`post`, or a file-like `save`), which confirms the class's 2026-09-04 reading: typing these receivers decides WHICH row (or a refusal) -- precision -- rather than reaching new rows -- recall. A slice's payoff figure must therefore come from the taint-path delta (0003's method: baseline clone vs subject, isolated caches, census of added AND removed flows, each adjudicated), not from slot counts.\n\nCANDIDATE SLICES, sized by this table and by what a static analyzer can derive:\n  (1) factory-function producers -- `x = f()` / `x = a.f()` / `f().m()` = 6,382 edges: the type is the project function's RETURN type, derivable when f is a project def with an annotation or a constructing return statement. Derivability NOT yet counted.\n  (2) self.<attr> chains -- 5,675: needs the field's type from __init__ assignments beyond the #756 constructor case (annotations, dataclass fields, Django model field classes). The Django ORM shape (`self.event.save()`) types to a project model, a SYMBOL not a module -- INV-kotob's cell -- so most of these would correctly carry NO module even when typed.\n  (3) parameters -- 3,358: annotation-only; the untyped majority is genuinely unrecoverable (WI-jokij's re-scope today, same conclusion from the other side).\nNEXT CENSUS BEFORE CODING: for (1), the share of callees that are project defs with a derivable return type; for (2), the share of fields typed by an annotation or a dataclass/model declaration. Whichever is larger AND has catalogued rows that are NOT ambiguous-name collisions is the first Phase 6 PR."  # 5d2a
- op: discuss  # 4976
  at: '2026-09-06T22:35:20Z'  # 4976
  by: agent  # 4976
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4976
  clock: 30  # 4976
  nonce: '4976'  # 4976
  message: "PHASE 6 DERIVABILITY CENSUS 2026-09-06 (dev 4f555a6fa9; population from the tip\nsurveys at 278d1c5fed), the census the 15:50 entry said must run before a slice is\nchosen. Reporting + the slice DECISION under the pre-registered rule; no code yet.\nInstrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/linub_derivability_09062026/ (PLAN.md written\nbefore the first number; derive.py; run_v2.out; two read-back rounds fixed four\ninstrument defects before any number was quoted: dotted constructors resolved by\ntheir root import, a callee's return type resolved in the DEF's file not the call\nsite's, builtin callees given their own bucket, typing.* treated as builtin).\n\nPOPULATION (unchanged): pretix 25,260 sentinel method edges (25,193 joined), kserve\n2,427 (2,406). Shapes under question: FACTORY inline f().m() 3,839 / 179, FACTORY\nbound x = f() 2,131 / 350, SELF self.<attr> chains 5,528 / 141.\n\nTHE 09-06 HYPOTHESIS WAS WRONG ABOUT WHERE THE TYPE IS. Project defs with a\nderivable return are SMALL: pretix F1 simple annotation 24, F2 non-simple 16,\nF3 constructing return 18, F4 underivable 187; own-__init__ fields typed by\nannotation/constructor/param 40. The type lives somewhere else:\n\n  1. THE DJANGO QUERYSET CHAIN -- 1,625 pretix method edges whose receiver is an\n     ORM chain (tallied across all shapes). py.py ALREADY types\n     `<Model>.objects.<m>()` (WI-sozoj, DJANGO_ORM_MODULE) but NOT the RESULT of\n     that call, so `X.objects.filter(...).exists()` loses the type at the second\n     hop: 942 sites rooted at `<Model>.objects`. The other 683 are chains whose\n     root is untyped (`self.event.items.filter(...).exists()`,\n     `request.auth.organizers.filter(...)`, `cp.addons.all().delete()`) and whose\n     only evidence is an intermediate QuerySet-method name. Terminal names:\n     exists 309, order_by 145, select_related 104, count 99, create_user 90,\n     filter 84, annotate 84, prefetch_related 82, delete 77, values 72, first 68,\n     update 59, get 58, values_list 53, select_for_update 41 ... By class:\n     976 catalogued DISTINCTIVE names (exists, order_by, select_related,\n     prefetch_related, annotate, values_list, first, exclude, ... = the RECALL\n     cell: the F3 gate refuses these method-kind rows today for want of a\n     module), 477 AMBIGUOUS names (get/all/count/delete/filter/update/values =\n     the PRECISION cell), 172 not catalogued (custom manager methods:\n     create_user, get_with_secret_check).\n  2. THE REVERSE-RELATION MANAGER -- 1,901 self.<attr> receivers whose field was\n     assigned from an ORM chain in setUp() (own 798, inherited base-class setUp\n     1,103): `self.orga = Organizer.objects.create(...)` then\n     `self.orga.events.create()`. The field types to a PROJECT model (no module,\n     correct) and the `.events` accessor is a RelatedManager knowable only from\n     Event.organizer = ForeignKey(related_name=\"events\") -- a project-wide\n     relation index py.py does not build. 1,159 distinctive-catalogued terminal\n     names, 264 ambiguous, 553 not catalogued. SECOND candidate.\n  3. super().<m>() -- 1,365 (project parent -> no module). 74 are save/delete;\n     33 sit in DIRECT models.Model subclasses (WI-sozoj's own gate could take\n     them), 23 via LoggedModel (a transitive base, which WI-sozoj deferred).\n  4. Framework BASE-CLASS attributes -- 1,263 self.<attr> never assigned in the\n     class or a project base (django 1,157: self.request/self.kwargs/self.object;\n     rest_framework 106: self.context/self.instance). A data gap (a base-class\n     attribute catalogue) with NO catalogued row to reach today (django.http is\n     not rowed). Not a candidate.\n  5. Third-party factory returns -- 614 (top: gettext_lazy 105, timezone.now 55,\n     gettext 48, get_template 48, get_redis_connection 29, b64encode 25, sha256\n     22): library_signatures/python.yaml has 16 rows and none of these; the\n     returned types are mostly str/datetime/Template -- non-I/O. Data gap, low\n     payoff. (One misclass: celery task `.apply()` on a project function, 32.)\n  6. Chains rooted at an untyped LOCAL -- 761; inherited method from an\n     unresolved base -- 203; getattr()-bound -- 10. Information absent at this\n     level (second-order: needs the local / the base typed first).\nkserve (the non-Django repo): NO recall cell of any kind -- getattr 124,\nthird-party returns unknown 122, untyped locals 136, super() 62. It is the\nCONTROL repository for the PR below: nothing should move there.\n\nDECISION under PLAN.md's rule (largest MECHANISM-GAP bucket whose derived types\nreach third-party catalogued rows): the first Phase 6 PR is QUERYSET CHAIN\nPROPAGATION, extending WI-sozoj in py.py:\n  (a) the RESULT of `<Model>.objects.<qs_method>()` carries DJANGO_ORM_MODULE, so\n      the next hop matches (942 sites; QS methods = the QuerySet-returning\n      subset of DJANGO_ORM_MANAGER_METHODS: filter/exclude/all/order_by/annotate/\n      select_related/prefetch_related/values/values_list/distinct/none/using/\n      only/defer/select_for_update -- NOT get/first/last/create, which return a\n      Model instance, a project class);\n  (b) propagation across consecutive QS methods (`.filter().exclude().exists()`);\n  (c) SEPARATELY GATED and separately measured: a chain whose root is untyped but\n      which passes through a DISTINCTIVE QS method name (select_related,\n      prefetch_related, exclude, values_list, annotate, order_by, distinct,\n      select_for_update, only, defer) types to DJANGO_ORM_MODULE from that hop\n      on; `filter`/`all` alone are ambiguous names and are NOT evidence unless the\n      file imports from django.db (framework gate). (c) is the by-name rule\n      INV-nular warns about, so it ships only if its read-back is clean.\nMEASUREMENT, pre-registered: the 0003 marginal-precision delta -- baseline clone\nat the merge base vs subject, isolated XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm, pretix (subject,\nthe only Django repo in the cohort) + kserve (control, expected 0 moved), the\ngeneric claims; EVERY added and removed flow adjudicated under ADR-0046's\ntwo-axis rubric with the CONFIGURED-ACTION test; expected shape = new db_read\nsources (exists/count/first/order_by...) and db_write sinks (delete/update) on\nuntrusted-input-no-database, i.e. the WI-vazal db_read->db_write shape, which\nthe adjudication prices rather than assumes. INV-karud's next pass (the pretix\nd3 repro) RIDES the same subject run. The PR carries awaits_bakeoff_validation.\nRefutation condition, written now: any site typed to django.db.models whose\nreceiver is NOT a Django manager/QuerySet in the read-back (a pandas `.filter`,\na project class defining `exclude`) counts against (c); one such site removes\nrule (c) from the PR."  # 4976
