- op: discuss  # 9c3d
  at: '2026-09-07T00:10:51Z'  # 9c3d
  by: agent  # 9c3d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9c3d
  clock: 32  # 9c3d
  nonce: 9c3d  # 9c3d
  message: "PHASE 6 PR 1 SHIPPED (branch jgstern-agent/feat/django-queryset-chain-typing; PR number in the reply below) -- QuerySet chain propagation. Implementation: the result of `<x>.objects.<queryset-method>()` carries DJANGO_ORM_MODULE (root rule in _preserved_receiver_type; the `.objects` receiver itself stays untyped so a project-defined manager method never gets a false owner path), 21 QuerySet-returning members as data in library_signatures/python.yaml so chained hops propagate through TYPE_PRESERVING_MEMBERS; get/first/create excluded (Model instance). Rule (c) (untyped-root, by name) NOT shipped. Seven tests. Full slice 10,779 passed; changed sources at 100%.\n\nMEASUREMENT 0013 (docs/measurements/0013-django-queryset-chain-delta.md; instrument ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mumov_qschain_09062026/), two arms, baseline asserted in the log (root rule 0 / rows 0 -> restored 1 / 21), isolated caches: kserve (control) 63 -> 63, 0 moved, 0 lost. pretix 102 -> 147 rows = 99 -> 139 situations: 40 NEW, 0 GONE, 31 with a moved representative (the 29 \"removed\" rows were re-keys -- the collapse now names a chained hop; LIVE rule 11). Every new situation read at source: L 28 = lazy combinator -> write (`filter(...).delete()`): TRUE by the 0001 rubric (the QuerySet is the receiver), VACUOUS: KIND-MISDECLARED under ADR-0046 -- the ADR-0049 lazy row WI-lunav kept, now removable under ruling 3 because this PR represents the executing reads; R-TP 7 = `select_for_update(...).get(pk=...)` -> generate_invoice/create, Voucher.create from the fetched entry, sync_order(sq.order), get_or_create(payment=payment); R-FP 5 = value does not travel (order_id selection, a pk passed, a read after the sink call). Correctness 87.5% (35/40), useful 17.5% (7/40); with the lazy rows fixed the same delta reads 7/12 = 58.3%. The refutation condition did not fire (no non-Django receiver typed). Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation. No verdict moved: every affected claim was violated in both arms.\n\nNEXT (Phase 6, filed in the reply below): the lazy QuerySet combinators leave the minting boundary (ADR-0049 ruling 3's licence is now met), positive control = the 28 L situations vanish and the 7 R-TP remain. Then the reverse-relation manager (candidate 2; two of the five FPs' real writes live there).\n\nThe lazy-combinator item: WI-fasap-zizoh-marov-lihob-jahuf-rosiv-tupuz-dusog."  # 9c3d
